)[
  == Smoked Paprika Salmon


  === Ingredients

  #ingredients[
    - Salmon, with skin -- 800 g
    - Olive oil -- 2 tbsp
    - Salt -- 1.5 tsp
    - Paprika powder --
    - Smoked paprika powder -- 
    - Black pepper, ground --
  ]

  === Preparation

  + Slice up the salmon fillets to a nice size for dining, or alternatively into smaller cubes for more crunchiness.
    Leaving the skin is highly recommended, as it's the tastiest bit!
  + Place in a large bowl and coat with olive oil.
  + Add generous amounts of smoked paprika and black pepper for the taste, some paprika for the colour, and some salt. Mix thoroughly.
  + Bake at 160 #sym.degree\C, with the skins facing up, for about 20 minutes or until golden. 

    #tip[I recommend baking with hot air convection. If you don't, the fillet sides might have little white bubbles, but will taste just as delicious.]
]
